# Code owners — dirwin/wp-site-uplinksync
#
# This GitLab is CE (Free): GitLab itself does NOT enforce "approval from code owners".
# Enforcement is the `owner_review_gate` job (tools/ci/owner_review_gate.py). It reads THIS
# FILE FROM THE MR's TARGET BRANCH, lists the MR's changed paths, and fails the MR pipeline
# unless @dirwin has approved the MR after its latest push whenever any changed path matches a
# rule below. With "Pipelines must succeed" on, a red gate blocks the merge.
#
# Everything NOT matched here (page/post content, docs, CSS, fonts, images, front-end JS,
# block templates/parts/patterns) is "low-risk": an MR labelled `low-risk` with a green
# pipeline and all threads resolved may be merged by the Paperclip agent token.
# Policy: docs/agent-merge-policy.md. Changing this file is itself owner-reviewed.
#
# Syntax (gitignore-like): leading "/" = repo root; trailing "/" = whole directory;
# "*" = within one path segment; "**" = any depth; a pattern without "/" matches a file
# or directory name at any depth.

